# Pre-mortem marker — cli#477 init banner collapse
- date: 2026-11-06
- branch: fix/init-banner-collapse
- mode: light (3 lenses)
- risk-ledger: inline (small scope; no separate ledger doc)

## edward-tufte — aggregation

- T1 Grouping too coarse hides a family that matters. FOLDED: .claude/ keeps
  two levels, because hooks, skills and rules are different kinds of thing.
- T2 Grouping too fine reproduces the defect at a new depth. FOLDED: standards/
  and scripts/ fold to one level; the test asserts under 30 group lines.
- T3 A group key that still names a file would look fixed but not be. FOLDED:
  the test rejects any key ending in a file extension.

## don-norman — feedback

- N4 Collapsing hides a real failure. FOLDED: refused, unchanged and errored
  counts all still print by default, and each names its flag.
- N5 Adopter cannot find the detail. FOLDED: the refused line says --verbose,
  and the --help text for --verbose now says what it carries.

## michael-feathers — characterization

- F6 Tests weakened to pass. FOLDED: both patterns are unchanged; only the
  invocation moved. Verified by hand against a real --verbose run.
- F7 File-set coverage lost. FOLDED: four new tests read
  .bassclef/init.manifest.json — outcome on every entry, SHA-256 on every
  created entry, and a refused entry when a target already exists.
- F8 Test count rises while a file silently fails to load. CHECKED: 542 tests
  / 231 suites before, 551 / 233 after. Both totals moved up by exactly what
  was added.
